.TH TDSETEST 1
.SH NAME
tdsetest \- check danby/tdse's solver against the closed form
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tdsetest
[
.B -v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IR Danby-tdse (1)
integrates the time-dependent Schrodinger equation through a barrier.
.IR Danby-tunnel (1)
gives the transmitted fraction for the same barrier from a formula.
They are worked out completely differently \(em one steps a field
forward in time, the other matches waves at two faces and never
integrates anything \(em so making them agree is worth considerably more
than either being self-consistent.
.PP
This reads the same spec file the program runs,
.BR /lib/danby/tdse.pde ,
and not a copy of it.
.SH "WHAT IT CHECKS"
.TP
.B The solver is unitary
The norm must not change.  It holds to about one part in 1e5 across
every run here, which is the one number that says the step is still
solving something.
.TP
.B It agrees with the formula
Measured against analytic, at barrier 10 and width 0.6: 0.079 against
0.071, 0.139 against 0.126, 0.235 against 0.219, 0.378 against 0.367,
0.557 against 0.569.
.TP
.B Transmission rises with energy, and falls with width
0.45, 0.13, 0.064 at widths 0.4, 0.8 and 1.2.
.TP
.B A barrier of zero height stops nothing
The control: without it, the width and energy checks would pass on a
model that reflected nothing ever.
.SH "WHY THE AGREEMENT IS NOT EXACT"
The reason is physical and not numerical, and it is why the test asserts
a bracket rather than a number.  The formula is for ONE energy.  A
packet is a spread of them, of width 1/(2 sigma) in k, and T varies
sharply across that spread.  So the measured fraction is required to lie
between the formula's values at the two ends of the packet's own
spectrum.
.PP
The sign of the disagreement is itself a check that nothing is wrong:
the measured value sits ABOVE the single-energy formula at low energy
and BELOW it at high, which is what averaging a curve of that shape over
a spread must do.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tdsetest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-tdse (1),
.IR danby-tunnel (1),
.IR pdehoctest (1),
.IR pde (2)
.SH BUGS
It runs for a fixed number of steps rather than detecting that the
packet has finished crossing, so changing the mesh or the barrier
position in the spec file will need that number changed with it.
.PP
Nothing here checks the picture.  It checks the field the picture is
drawn from.
